Vendored upstream source
------------------------

The directory vendor/YMPublic/ contains files copied without modification
from the Yang-Mills group's results repository:

  Repository: https://github.com/yang-mills-group/YM
  Commit:     319ecd5274241200b27bb5b143a59133fd670ea6 (2026-11-25)
  Path:       submissions/openai-20261028/submission/

  PublicTheory.lean   sha256 94111ad258b4218a263fcc0a7136446d5a6eff0e090809b72036fb3a7aecfff8
  PublicWilson.lean   sha256 c1542c816cd42d23448b66b4cb021c7f3bdad64b64f1c643dde27147ce0c3233
  ChallengeSpec.lean  sha256 e48b0be2b72d16b9b87c6c1923b3ae814270387bf9312b5cb0661dfa3e243749

These three hashes match the upstream file
submissions/openai-20261028/submission/verification/challenge.sha256.

The upstream files are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Their
LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD_PARTY.md are kept beside them in vendor/YMPublic/
and continue to apply. The upstream NOTICE records that the public gauge,
Wightman and OPE interfaces adapt earlier challenge sources at revision
eea94292e31734d46498be7836d7e8fa50ca8cd2.

provenance.json records the upstream paths and the SHA-256 of every vendored
file.

Dependencies
------------

The Lean project depends on Lean 4 (leanprover/lean4:v4.32.0) and Mathlib
(rev 81a5d257c8e410db227a6665ed08f64fea08e997), both Apache-2.0, fetched by
Lake at build time and not included in this repository.

